  "id": "dukotah-h03-onion-cookie-xor",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Do the onion cookies reveal text by XOR?",
  "question": "Does the exact source-executed cookie-to-blob XOR grid produce any 32-byte output with at least 80% printable ASCII?",
  "reader_question": "Have the 2013 onion cookies been XORed against the grid and later blobs?",
  "summary": "The executable 64-case source grid reproduces a null at its printable threshold; the written plan describes additional cases and checks that this executable did not run.",
  "finding": "Across two decoded cookies, four 256-byte objects and eight aligned 32-byte blocks each, zero of 64 XOR outputs reaches 26/32 printable bytes; the maximum is 20/32. A planted 32-byte ASCII block is detected by the original source function. A retrospective source-helper/strict-padding/named-prefix diagnostic finds zero matches on the same 64 outputs and recovers all three synthetic controls.",
  "limitations": "The raw-cookie arm cannot be reconstructed from the written plan: 64 ASCII characters versus 32-byte blocks with no alignment rule. The broader digest/string set and encoding are unspecified. The pinned executable implements only 64 hex-decoded cases. The supplementary PKCS and one-prefix checks are retrospective, exact-predicate diagnostics, not the original source run.",
  "next_steps": "Specify the raw-cookie interpretation and exact digest or padding targets before treating the full written H-03 plan as executed.",
  "outcome": "not-supported",
